<%# The training commitment as a badge. With T7 the card got a second
    consumer (the switch dialog). That is the same point at which the
    jurisdiction badge was extracted: a colour rule with two handwritten
    copies is one copy too many.

    The colours come from AiPackage::TRAINING_USAGE_BADGE_STYLES, so a new
    value does not silently fall into a grey badge. Unlike the jurisdiction
    case, the constant works directly for the customer side here: green, red,
    grey are already the colours fit for customers (D4).

    Empty value = NO badge, not a grey one. That is the self_hosted case
    (and in the dialog also „Eigene Konfiguration"): there the question
    does not apply, it is not unanswered. A grey badge would be a warning
    about nobody.

    Local: training_usage (String or nil). %>
<% if training_usage.present? %>
  <span class="inline-flex items-center px-2 py-1 rounded text-xs font-bold border border-ink <%= AiPackage::TRAINING_USAGE_BADGE_STYLES[training_usage] %>">
    <%= t("views.organisations.ai_settings.packages.training_usages.#{training_usage}") %>
  </span>
<% end %>
